{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5940b452-3738-468a-9ce8-e248fd7f49c2",
    "name": "Scheduled Notification Dispatcher",
    "description": "Scheduled notification dispatcher \u2014 API, mock provider and a live dispatch run.\n\n## Before you start\n\n```\ndocker compose up -d          # Postgres on 5433\ndb/apply.sh --reset           # hand-written schema\nnpm run provider              # mock provider on 4010\nnpm run api                   # api on 3100\nnpm run worker                # worker 1\nnpm run worker                # worker 2 (second terminal)\n```\n\n## Folders\n\n| Folder | Needs | Shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 \u00b7 Health | api + provider | the right processes are answering |\n| 1 \u00b7 Campaign lifecycle | api | A1, A2, A3 and the second-cancel no-op |\n| 2 \u00b7 Live dispatch | api + 2 workers + provider | messages actually going out, nothing stuck |\n| 3 \u00b7 Mock provider | provider | P1, P2, P3 and the key-before-dice ordering |\n| 4 \u00b7 Validation | api | every rejection path |\n\nFolders 0, 1, 3 and 4 run without workers. Folder 2 needs them.\n\nEvery request asserts the rule it demonstrates, so running the collection is a check, not a demo.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "apiUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3100",
      "description": "Port 3100, not 3000 \u2014 3000 collides with other local services."
    },
